#N canvas 20 20 1620 1340 12;
#X text 20 20 u_oled-preview -- shows what the patch draws to the OLED \, off-device. Instantiated by u_mother-stub only. Eight boxes \, one per 8-pixel ROW of the 128x64 screen \, keyed by the y coordinate of each gPrintln., f 58;
#X text 20 115 Not five boxes: screenLine1-5 is a DIFFERENT api \, the five text lines mother.pd offers a patch \, and u_mother-stub previews those separately. This is the graphics api \, which is pixel-positioned. 64 pixels over an 8px font is 8 rows., f 58;
#X text 20 230 It shows WHAT is drawn and ROUGHLY where -- the row it starts on. Not a framebuffer: a 24px line covers three rows but only registers in the one it starts in., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 r oscOut;
#X obj 20 340 route sendtyped;
#X obj 400 380 print oscOut-not-sendtyped;
#X obj 20 410 route /oled/gPrintln /oled/gClear;
