#X obj 860 590 + 1;
#X floatatom 700 620 7 0 0 0 - - -;
#X text 20 830 row 0 -- y 0-7 -- the L level starts here, f 22;
#X text 200 830 row 1, f 22;
#X text 380 830 row 2, f 22;
#X text 560 830 row 3 -- y 24-31 -- the R level, f 22;
#X text 740 830 row 4, f 22;
#X text 920 830 row 5 -- the self-test draws here, f 22;
#X text 1100 830 row 6 -- y 48-55 -- the status word, f 22;
#X text 1280 830 row 7, f 22;
#X text 20 960 The row is y divided by 8 \, so any layout lands somewhere sensible without editing this file. That matters for Phase 3 \, which is the phase that changes where things get drawn., f 46;
#X text 540 960 gClear does NOT blank the previews. The display redraws ten times a second \, so blanking would only produce flicker -- and the last text per row is the useful thing. The counter is the liveness indicator instead., f 46;
#X text 1060 960 THE t b IS LOAD-BEARING. route emits gClear's arguments \, ii 3 1 \, and feeding that straight to a float inlet prints float: no method for 'ii' ten times a second \, forever., f 46;
#X text 20 1090 SELF-TEST -- click these and watch the boxes above. Row 5 is deliberately a row nothing else draws to \, so the first one STAYS. The other two do not change a box: gClear only bumps the counter \, and gFilledCircle is unhandled and goes to the console., f 58;
#X msg 640 1090 sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiisi 3 4 40 8 1 hello 42;
#X msg 640 1130 sendtyped /oled/gClear ii 3 1;
#X msg 640 1170 sendtyped /oled/gFilledCircle iiiii 3 10 10 8 1;
